Here's a simple Discord bot using Discord.js v14 with a `ban` command:

```javascript
const { RichClient } = require('discord.js');
const client = new RichClient();

client.on('ready', () => {
  console.log(`Logged in as ${client.user.tag}`);
});

client.on('message', (message) => {
  if (message.content.startsWith('!ban')) {
    const user = message.content.slice(6);
    if (!user) return;

    const member = message.guild.members.find(m => m.tag === user);
    if (!member) return;

    member.ban({ reason: 'Banned by bot' });
    message.channel.send(`Banned ${user}`);
  }
});

client.login('YOUR_BOT_TOKEN');
```

This bot listens for messages that start with `!ban` and then extracts the user's tag from the message content. It then finds the user in the guild and bans them with a reason "Banned by bot". Finally, it sends a message to the channel indicating that the user has been banned.

Note: Make sure to replace `'YOUR_BOT_TOKEN'` with your actual bot token. You can get the token from the Discord Developer Portal.

Also, make sure to give the necessary permissions to your bot to ban other users.

